## Domain Philosophy

- Domain objects model **business behavior**, not data storage
- They are deterministic, explicit, and testable

---

## Allowed in Domain Objects

- Plain Ruby
- Value objects
- Explicit state transitions
- Raising domain-relevant exceptions
- Deterministic algorithms

---

## Forbidden in Domain Objects

- ActiveRecord
- Database access
- Transactions
- External services (HTTP, APIs)
- Background jobs
- Logging frameworks

---

## Initialization Rules

- Domain objects must be initialized with everything they need
- No hidden dependencies
- No global state

---

## Error Handling

- Domain objects may raise
- They do NOT rescue infrastructure errors
- Repositories decide how to persist failures

---

## Specs as Contracts

- Domain specs are authoritative
- If specs are unclear, STOP and ask
- Never "fix" specs by loosening behavior

---

## Determinism Guarantee

- Same input → same output
- No randomness unless explicitly specified
